// case: config-port-zero
// what: a `port` config declaration outside the TCP port range.
//
// 0 is the classic "pick any free port" value in socket APIs, but Orbit's
// declaration promises the port the service will be on, and the banner and
// the docs both quote it. A server that lands somewhere the declaration does
// not name makes that promise a lie, so 0 is out of range here; only 1..65535
// are ports a service can actually declare.
port 0
// expect-error: out of range: a TCP port is 1 to 65535
